AB  - Hemocytic defense response of the migratory grasshopper, Melanoplus sanguinipes (Fab.), to conidia of the white muscardine fungus, Beauveria bassiana (Bals.) Vuill., was studied using phase-contrast photomicroscopy, hemocyte counting and hemocyte aggregation or 'nodule formation'. Grasshoppers were injected with an aqueous suspension of conidia. Adherence of B. bassiana conidia to granulocytes occurred within 10 min and the conidia were encapsulated by these hemocytes 6 h postinjection. Hemocytopenia was accompanied by nodule formation after injection of B. bassiana conidia into grasshoppers. The conidia germinated within the nodules and grew into hyphal forms within the hemolymph 12 to 24 h postinjection. We conclude that B. bassiana competes well with nodule formation by hemocytes of M. sanguinipes and often escapes complete encapsulation.
