AB  - The strain of Beauveris bassiana (Bala) Vuill was separated from the corpse of Rhytidodera bowringii White which has been infected naturally. After purification, a large number of colony was produced and used to control R. bowringii White. Two methods were adopted in this test, one is blocking up the pest with suspension liquid of B. bassiana, the other is inoculation using injector to drip the suspension liquid into the body. The results show that seven days later, by the method of blocking up, the average death percentage is 70.6%, in which the death percentage of larvae is 87.5%, of pupae and adults is 36.7%. By the method of inoculation, the average death percentage is 66.1%, in which the death percentage of larvae is 82.5%, of pupae and adults is 33.3%. These two methods were conducted on 27 years old mango trees(13.3hm~(2)), the effect of control is 83.7%. After application on 15 years old mango trees (35.0hm~(2)), the effect of control is 84.1%.
